		(property "Wright.PickReason" "2026-11-03 Aluminium electrolytic / hybrid capacitor x2: needs V rated >= 80V, C >= 1.49mF. jlcparts Active (catalog status field (JLC/LCSC listing, not the manufacturer)), stock 852, 1.5490 USD each at 2. V rated 80V meets min 80V; C 1.5mF meets min 1.49mF (0 other candidates passed) Chosen because: Specified by you: Rubycon ZLH 80 V 1500 uF radial, 18x40 mm, 7.5 mm pitch, lies flat. 80 V = 1.85x the 43.2 V charge voltage. Lifecycle basis is the JLC/LCSC catalogue only (Digi-Key/Mouser keys off, research pages bot-blocked); introduction date and successor not found, age unverified. Ripple rating read from the Rubycon ZLH datasheet (the JLC-hosted PDF, page 3, rendered and read by eye): 80 V 1500 uF 18x40 = 3510 mA rms at 105 C, 100 kHz, impedance 0.026 ohm max at 20 C 100 kHz; frequency multiplier for 820-1800 uF is 0.60 at 120 Hz, 0.80 at 1 kHz, 0.96 at 10 kHz, 1.00 at 100 kHz and up. Two caps = about 7.0 A rms total at 100 kHz and above, less at lower frequency. That is the number the ~13 A/channel continuous claim rests on; the real bus ripple depends on motor current, modulation and the 3 x 2.2 uF ceramics per half-bridge, which are not modelled yet, so it is NOT qualified. Datasheet gives no introduction date; the ZLH is a long-running Rubycon series and no successor was found."
			(at 119.38 88.9 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1 1)
				)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
