		(property "Wright.PickReason" "2026-11-05 MOSFET x12 (Q1-Q12): needs Vds >= 100V, Id >= 60A, Rds(on) <= 5.5mΩ. jlcparts Active (catalog status field (JLC/LCSC listing, not the manufacturer)), stock 2915, 0.9671 USD each at 12. Vds 100V meets min 100V; Id 100A meets min 60A; Rds(on) 5.1mΩ meets max 5.5mΩ. Design-in: no open design in the corpus uses it. Freshness: catalogue freshness 0.00 (C7363870 is in the newest 54% of 19,524 listings in MOSFETs + Silicon Carbide Field Effect Transistor (MOSFET)). (24 other candidates passed; 7 other candidates on the shortlist) Chosen because: Motor half-bridge FETs, replaces STL90N10F7 (refused, 2013). Flags come from parts constraints (43.2 V bus, 30 A, 45 A peak) plus Rds(on) <= 5.5 mOhm so burst loss drops from the old part's 10.5 mOhm. Vishay datasheet doc 63091 rev C, 04-Dec-2023, TrenchFET Gen V, PowerPAK SO-8: 100 V, 4.5 mOhm max at 10 V, Qg 41 nC typ and 62 nC max at 10 V, Vgs(th) 2-4 V, RthJC 1.3 C/W max, 100 A package limit, pin 1-3 S, 4 G, 5-8 D. Chosen over BSC027N10NS5 because the catalogue shows 4.17 USD against 0.97, 785 in stock against 2,915 and Qg 89 nC against 62 nC max; its lower catalogue Rds(on) of 2.1 mOhm is not worth 4x cost at 13 A continuous. Chosen over BSC034N10LS5 because the catalogue states its Qg at 4.5 V, which marks a logic-level part with less threshold margin against dV/dt turn-on in a hard-switched bridge, and it has 511 in stock. Chosen over the lesser-known PDFN shortlist rows because no maker tables were read for them and the Vishay tables were. Footprint: Package_SO:PowerPAK_SO-8_Single, the KiCad library pattern (kicad-footprints Package_SO.pretty/PowerPAK_SO-8_Single.kicad_mod, drawn from Vishay doc 71655 outline and doc 72599 recommended minimum pads: lead pads 0.61 x 1.27 mm at 1.27 mm pitch, drain body 3.81 x 3.91 mm plus four 0.61 x 1.02 mm drain leads), swapped on the board and the schematic on 2026-11-05 in place of the ST-derived Wright:PowerFLAT-8_5x6mm_ST-typeR; the 24 VBUS thermal vias on Q1-Q3 and Q7-Q9 sit at footprint-local (-0.06 or 2.14, +/-1.10) mm with 0.40 mm radius, fully inside the 3.81 x 3.91 mm drain body, and kicad-cli DRC with refilled zones gave errors 0 and unconnected 291 both before and after the swap. 30 A at 4.5 mOhm is about 4 W per conducting FET before temperature rise: an estimate, not a thermal qualification. No open design in the corpus uses it; lifecycle basis is the JLC catalogue only, Digi-Key and Mouser keys are off. Gate: lifecycle Unknown: jlcparts listing lists it, which is a catalogue listing, not a manufacturer status; no manufacturer lifecycle source is configured (no Digi-Key or Mouser key in parts.json), so the gate cannot prove Active; introduction date unknown (no datasheet first date, research report or curated row), so the age rule could not run || Correction 2026-11-06 (motor1_power_stage review, turn 3 by the host): Q1-Q6 are picked back to SIR512DP-T1-RE3, the same part as Q7-Q12, so both motors use one FET as the spec requires (motor2_power_stage needs.same_as). The 11-06 re-pick to onsemi NVMFWS015N10MCLT1G is withdrawn: it was searched with only the derived flags (Vds >= 100 V, Id >= 40 A) and dropped the Rds(on) <= 5.5 mOhm bound of the 11-05 pick; its Rds(on) is 12.2 mOhm max against 5.1 mOhm (about 11 W per FET at a 30 A burst) and its Id is 29.8 A at Tc 100 C against the 30 A phase peak, so it had no current margin. Its claim that SIR512DP-T1-RE3 was not on the shortlist was wrong: `wright parts search --kind mosfet --vds-min 100 --id-min 40 --package DFN5x6` lists SIR512DP-T1-RE3 on the shortlist. Footprint restored to Package_SO:PowerPAK_SO-8_Single (Vishay doc 72599 pattern, the footprint the block was routed on) on the sheet and the board; the 488AA footprint file is deleted from Wright.pretty."
			(at 152.4 53.34 0)
