		(property "Wright.PickReason" "2026-11-03 Rectifier / Schottky diode x6: needs Vr >= 40V, If >= 150mA. jlcparts Active (catalog status field (JLC/LCSC listing, not the manufacturer)), stock 89940, 0.0179 USD each at 6. Vr 200V meets min 40V; If 250mA meets min 150mA (5095 other candidates passed) Chosen because: Motor-1 gate turn-off diodes (one per FET, in series with R7-R12, across the turn-on resistor). Gate swing is 12 V, so Vr >= 40 V has margin (BAS321 is rated 200 V, 250 mA). Nexperia, 89,940 in JLC stock; the review dates it 4 years from its datasheet (under the 10-year line); no successor named in the catalogue. Lifecycle basis is the JLC catalogue only (Digi-Key and Mouser keys are off), so it stays flagged watch; any equivalent SOD-323 small-signal switching diode is an acceptable second source."
