		(property "Description" "8-Bit Single-Supply Bus Transceiver With 5V tolerant input voltage and 3-State Outputs 24mA, TSSOP-20"
			(at 203.2 129.54 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1 1)
				)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
		(property "MPN" "DRV8300UDPWR"
			(at 203.2 129.54 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1 1)
				)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
		(property "Manufacturer" "Texas Instruments"
			(at 203.2 129.54 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1 1)
				)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
		(property "Wright.PickReason" "2026-11-03 Gate driver x2: needs no electrical constraint. jlcparts Active (catalog status field (JLC/LCSC listing, not the manufacturer)), stock 79, 1.9309 USD each at 2.  (1287 other candidates passed) Chosen because: Motor-1 three-phase gate driver (motor 2 reuses it as the second DRV8300UDPWR, board total 2). Constraints: three half-bridges in one IC, SHx/BSTx rated >= 100 V on a 43.2 V pack (datasheet: SHx 100 V, BSTx abs max 125 V), runs from the 12 V gate rail (GVDD 5-20 V), UVLO on GVDD and BST (rising 8.3 V / BSTUV 8 V typ, tuned for standard 10 V MOSFETs), integrated bootstrap diodes (DRV8300UD, so no external bootstrap diodes are needed), 750 mA source / 1.5 A sink, fixed 200 ns dead-time and interleaved-conduction lockout as backup to the STM32G4 advanced-timer dead-time. TI DRV8300U datasheet SLVSGY3B (Jul 2022, rev Jun 2025) read for these figures. Variant caveat: the TSSOP-20 DRV8300UD has an INVERTED low-side input (GLx = not INLx); the non-inverted DRV8300UDI is not in the catalogue, so the STM32 low-side CHxN polarity must be set inverted in firmware, or the schematic phase must check it. Lifecycle: TI product page ACTIVE/Production, introduced July 2022 (research report research/DRV8300UDPWR.json, status_source_kind manufacturer); no successor named (DRV8300 and DRV8363 on the page are alternates). Age 4 years, under the 10-year line. Stock: JLC 79 vs 2 needed; Digi-Key/Mouser stock not read (keys off). Prior art: memirmakar/foc-driver (STM32G431 + DRV8300DPWR, BOM_revB.csv and HANDOVER.md) uses 33 ohm turn-on / 10 ohm + diode turn-off gate resistors, 1 uF 25 V X7R bootstrap, 10 uF 25 V GVDD decoupling and 2x 2.2 uF 100 V 1210 per leg; it is a small two-commit Rev B project, so it is a design reference, not proof."
			(at 203.2 129.54 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1 1)
				)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
		(property "Wright.Source" "jlcparts C7172549"
			(at 203.2 129.54 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1 1)
				)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
		(property "Wright.Note" "DRV8300UDPWR (UD, 20-pin TSSOP): LS input INLx is INVERTED (GLx = not INLx), so the MCU low-side outputs run inverted polarity; floating INHx/INLx pull the outputs low (datasheet 8.3.2). No nFAULT pin: overcurrent trip comes from the block-5 comparators to BKIN. GND pin to board GND, not the shunt side. Symbol Wright:DRV8300UD_TSSOP20 is a derived pin map (no TI symbol installed); footprint Package_SO:TSSOP-20_4.4x6.5mm_P0.65mm to be checked against the PW package drawing."
			(at 203.2 129.54 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1 1)
				)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
