			)
		)
		(property "Manufacturer" "Texas Instruments"
			(at 80.01 129.54 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1 1)
				)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
		(property "Wright.PickReason" "2026-11-03 Gate driver x2: needs no electrical constraint. jlcparts Active (catalog status field (JLC/LCSC listing, not the manufacturer)), stock 79, 1.9309 USD each at 2.  (1287 other candidates passed) Chosen because: Motor-2 three-phase gate driver, the same DRV8300UDPWR as motor 1 U2 (board total 2, stock 79 at JLC, so 2 are covered). SHx 100 V, BSTx abs max 125 V, runs from the 12 V gate rail (GVDD 5-20 V), UVLO on GVDD/BST, integrated bootstrap diodes (so no external bootstrap diodes), 750 mA source / 1.5 A sink, fixed 200 ns dead-time and interleaved-conduction lockout as backup to the STM32G4 dead-time. TI datasheet SLVSGY3B. The TSSOP-20 DRV8300UD has an inverted low-side input, so the STM32 low-side CHxN polarity must be set inverted in firmware. Lifecycle: TI product page ACTIVE/Production, introduced July 2022 (research/DRV8300UDPWR.json, status_source_kind manufacturer), no successor named (DRV8300 and DRV8363 are alternates, not successors). Age 4 years. Digi-Key/Mouser stock not read (keys off). Prior art memirmakar/foc-driver (STM32G431 + DRV8300) as noted on U2."
			(at 80.01 129.54 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1 1)
				)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
		(property "Wright.Source" "jlcparts C7172549"
			(at 80.01 129.54 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1 1)
				)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
		(property "Wright.Note" "Same as motor 1 U2: DRV8300UDPWR (UD, 20-pin TSSOP) has an INVERTED low-side input (GLx = not INLx), floating INHx/INLx pull the outputs low (datasheet 8.3.2), no nFAULT pin, GND pin to board GND. Symbol Wright:DRV8300UD_TSSOP20 is a derived pin map (no TI symbol installed); footprint to be checked against the PW package drawing."
			(at 80.01 129.54 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1 1)
				)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
