		(property "Description" "Texas Instruments LM5164DDAR: 6-100 V input, 1 A synchronous COT buck converter, 8-pin PowerPAD SO (DDA); here 12 V out from VBUS"
			(at 69.85 39.37 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1 1)
				)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
		(property "MPN" "LM5164DDAR"
			(at 69.85 39.37 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1 1)
				)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
		(property "Manufacturer" "Texas Instruments"
			(at 69.85 39.37 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1 1)
				)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
		(property "Wright.PickReason" "2026-11-03 Buck / DC-DC converter IC x1: needs Vin >= 80V, Iout >= 500mA. jlcparts Active (catalog status field (JLC/LCSC listing, not the manufacturer)), stock 10908, 2.3604 USD each at 1. Vin 100V meets min 80V; Iout 1A meets min 500mA (66 other candidates passed) Chosen because: 12 V gate rail from VBUS (also the input of the 3.3 V stage). Constraints derived before searching: Vin(max) >= 80 V (pack 43.2 V charged, bus TVS clamps at 77 V, bulk caps 80 V, so a 100 V part keeps margin over the clamp; a 40-60 V buck would not), Iout >= 0.5 A (gate drive is about 12 FETs x 39 nC x 20-50 kHz = tens of mA, plus the 3.3 V stage; a linear regulator would burn about 3 W dropping 43 V, so a buck), fixed 12 V from a resistor divider, synchronous with no external diode, PGOOD. TI LM5164DDAR: 6-100 V in, 1 A, SO-8-EP, 12 V / 1 A / 300 kHz is the datasheet's own typical application (TI LM5164 datasheet SNVSAU4 section 7.2, figure 7-1 and table 7-1, rev Feb 2026, first release Sep 2018), so every passive of this block is copied from it: L 68 uH, Cin 2.2 uF 100 V, Cout 2 x 22 uF 25 V, Cbst 2.2 nF, Ron 100 k (300 kHz), Rfb1 453 k / Rfb2 49.9 k, ripple-injection Ra 453 k + Ca 3.3 nF + Cb 56 pF. Prior art: no open-source board using the LM5164 was found (web search found only library entries), so the precedent is TI's datasheet application and its EVM, not a third-party project. Age: about 8 years from the Sep 2018 first release, under the 10-year line. Lifecycle: JLC catalogue Active with 10,908 in stock; the host research report should add the TI page; Digi-Key/Mouser keys are off so manufacturer lifecycle was not checked in the catalogue. Successor: none named by the catalogue (the LM5164-Q1 variant is the automotive twin, not a successor). Loop stability, ripple and EMI are NOT verified, only copied from the reference design."
			(at 69.85 39.37 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1 1)
				)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
		(property "Wright.Source" "jlcparts C477928"
			(at 69.85 39.37 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1 1)
				)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
		(property "Wright.Note" "Topology is TI SNVSAU4 Figure 7-1 / Table 7-1 (12 V, 1 A, 300 kHz): EN/UVLO tied to VIN (datasheet 6.3.9 allows it, no input UVLO programmed), RON 100 k, FB divider 453 k / 49.9 k, Type-3 ripple injection RA 453 k + CA 3.3 nF from SW to VOUT with CB 56 pF into FB, CBST 2.2 nF, 2 x 2.2 uF in, 2 x 22 uF out, L 68 uH. Frequency is set for 48 V in; at the 39.6-43.2 V pack it differs (on-time scales with Vin). PGOOD left open (NC with datasheet reason). Symbol Wright:LM5164DDA is derived from the installed LMR36510ADDA symbol for its DDA package only; pin names/types are from the LM5164 datasheet Table 4-1. Footprint is KiCad's Texas HTSOP-8-1EP (TI DDA); check its pad against the LM5164 DDA drawing."
			(at 69.85 39.37 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1 1)
				)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
