		(property "Wright.PickReason" "2026-11-03 Power inductor x1: needs L = 68uH, Isat >= 1.8A, Irms >= 1A. jlcparts Active (catalog status field (JLC/LCSC listing, not the manufacturer)), stock 368, 0.9966 USD each at 1. L 68uH meets = 68uH; Isat 2.78A meets min 1.8A; Irms 2.49A meets min 1A (85 other candidates passed) Chosen because: LM5164 output inductor, 68 uH per the TI 12 V / 1 A reference design (datasheet table 7-1: 68 uH, 170 mOhm, > 1.8 A). Isat must exceed the LM5164 high-side peak current limit of 1.5 A typ (datasheet section 6, current limit; valley limit set to 1.2 A), so >= 1.8 A. Taiyo Yuden NS12575T680MN: Isat 2.78 A, Irms 2.49 A, 72 mOhm, 12.5 x 12.5 x 7.5 mm shielded, 368 in stock at JLC. Lifecycle evidence: a Taiyo Yuden datasheet copy lists Mass Production and Abacus lists Active/Mature (not a Digi-Key page for this exact part; Digi-Key and Mouser keys are off), so it stays flagged watch. SWAPPED FROM TDK SPM10054T-680M-HZ: Digi-Key (KR/FI listings) shows that part Not For New Designs; its named replacement SPM10054T-680M-HZR is Active at Digi-Key DE (Isat 3.2 A, 163 mOhm max, 10.7 x 10 mm, 15 wk lead) but the parts catalogue does not list it, so the pick tool cannot accept it; it is the smaller drop-in-class alternative to verify and use at layout time if the 12.5 mm footprint is too big. Also rejected: Coilcraft MSS1038-683MLC (Isat only 1.6 A at 20 percent drop, under the converter's 1.5 A peak limit plus tolerance) . The Active/Mature label means check last-time-buy notices before ordering."
			(at 96.52 36.83 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1 1)
				)
				(hide yes)
			)
