		(property "Wright.PickReason" "2026-11-03 Current-sense resistor x6: needs R = 2mΩ, P >= 2W. jlcparts Active (catalog status field (JLC/LCSC listing, not the manufacturer)), stock 11589, 0.3072 USD each at 6. R 2mΩ meets = 2mΩ; P 3W meets min 2W (76 other candidates passed) Chosen because: Low-side shunts, 2 mOhm 1% 3 W 2512, one per phase leg (R29-R31 motor 1, R32-R34 motor 2). Chosen with INA240A1 gain 20: 2 mOhm x 20 = 40 mV/A, +/-1.55 V around 1.65 V = +/-38 A, above the 30 A burst. Dissipation: 13 A rms continuous is 0.34 W, 30 A burst is 1.8 W, both under 3 W; 50 ppm/C. 2512 pads need Kelvin sense traces to the amplifier. Provisional: the phase-current waveform, duty and the burst length are not given, so thermal and the value itself are NOT qualified. Yageo PA2512FKE7T0R002E, JLC 11,589 in stock (passive, catalogue basis)."
			(at 153.67 91.44 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1 1)
				)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
		(property "Wright.Source" "jlcparts C375692"
			(at 153.67 91.44 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1 1)
				)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
		(property "Wright.Note" "2 mOhm 2512 two-terminal shunt (Yageo PA2512FKE7T0R002E) with INA240A1 gain 20 gives 40 mV/A (+/-38 A, above the 30 A burst). The spec's 1 mOhm starting value was replaced by 2 mOhm for ADC resolution; not qualified. Footprint R_2512_6332Metric is the generic pattern: check against the Yageo land pattern, and route the amplifier inputs as a Kelvin pair from the inner pad edges."
			(at 153.67 91.44 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1 1)
				)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
