		(property "Description" "Texas Instruments INA240A1PWR: bidirectional current-sense amplifier, gain 20 V/V, -4 to 80 V common mode, enhanced PWM rejection, 8-pin TSSOP (PW)"
			(at 31.75 185.42 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1 1)
				)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
		(property "MPN" "INA240A1PWR"
			(at 31.75 185.42 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1 1)
				)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
		(property "Manufacturer" "Texas Instruments"
			(at 31.75 185.42 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1 1)
				)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
		(property "Wright.PickReason" "2026-11-03 Current-sense amplifier x6: needs no electrical constraint. jlcparts Active (catalog status field (JLC/LCSC listing, not the manufacturer)), stock 2253, 2.6800 USD each at 6.  (253 other candidates passed) Chosen because: Phase-current amplifiers, one per low-side shunt (U5-U7 motor 1 phases A-C, U8-U10 motor 2). Constraints derived before searching: bidirectional with a mid-scale output (REF1 to VS, REF2 to GND gives VS/2 = 1.65 V on the 3.3 V rail, no reference IC needed; datasheet section 8.4.3), 2.7-5.5 V supply, common-mode range covering a low-side shunt including negative source spikes during diode conduction (INA240: -4 V to 80 V), enhanced PWM rejection, gain 20 V/V so 2 mOhm x 20 = 40 mV/A gives +/-1.55 V = about +/-38 A, above the 30 A burst. TI INA240A1PWR, TSSOP-8, bandwidth 400 kHz. Lifecycle: TI product page ACTIVE with no NRND or successor notice (research/INA240A1PWR.json, manufacturer page read by the lead worker); JLC stock 2,253 vs 6 needed. AGE: datasheet first dated July 2016, so about 10 years, at the 10-year line, not over it. SUCCESSOR CHECK: TI's page lists INA241B as a drop-in with upgraded functionality (a comparison suggestion, not a formal successor notice); the catalogue carries INA241 only as gain 10 (stock 49-263 at 4.4-5.3 USD) and 50-200 V/V, no gain-20 variant, so it cannot replace this part without a 4 mOhm shunt and a re-derivation, left as a respin option. Prior art: sirojudinMunir/sf-motion Hardware/Inverter.kicad_sch uses INA240A1PW (TSSOP-8) per phase with a 1 k series output resistor (I read only the first 100k characters, so its REF wiring and shunt value were not confirmed). Offset and gain error and shunt heating are not qualified."
			(at 31.75 185.42 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1 1)
				)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
		(property "Wright.Source" "jlcparts C93965"
			(at 31.75 185.42 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1 1)
				)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
		(property "Wright.Note" "Pinout is the PW (TSSOP-8) numbering from TI SBOS662C Table 6-1: 1 NC, 2 IN+ (supply side of shunt), 3 IN- (load side), 4 GND, 5 VS, 6 REF2, 7 REF1, 8 OUT; the SOIC D package numbers pins differently. REF1 to VS and REF2 to GND give a VS/2 midpoint (1.65 V on 3.3 V). Symbol Wright:INA240A1PW is a pin-shape stand-in derived from an installed TSSOP-8 symbol; names and types are from the datasheet. IN+ is the low-side FET source net (M*_SL_x), IN- is board GND at the shunt: route both as a Kelvin pair from the shunt pads."
			(at 31.75 185.42 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1 1)
				)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
