		(property "Wright.PickReason" "2026-11-05 Power inductor x1: needs L = 3.9uH, Isat >= 3.88A, Irms >= 2.5A. jlcparts Active (catalog status field (JLC/LCSC listing, not the manufacturer)), stock 208, 0.3525 USD each at 1. L 3.9uH meets = 3.9uH; Isat 3.9A meets min 3.88A; Irms 3.3A meets min 2.5A. Design-in: no open design in the corpus uses it. Freshness: catalogue freshness 0.00 (C19947652 is in the newest 21% of 23,355 listings in Power Inductors + Inductors (SMD)). (9 other candidates passed; 7 other candidates on the shortlist) Chosen because: AP63203 output inductor, replaces the 10 uH part chosen for the TPS54202. 3.9 uH comes from Diodes DS41326 table 2 for 3.3 V. Isat floor is 1.25 x the 3.1 A max HS peak limit, Irms floor is 2 A / 0.8, from parts constraints. Chosen because Bourns SRN6028C-3R9M is shortlist first with catalogue Isat 3.9 A, 3.3 A rated, 28 mOhm, +/-20 percent, 208 in stock, 6 x 6 mm, against ANR5040T3R9M with no DCR stated, FNR5040S3R9NT at +/-30 percent, and the larger 8 x 8 mm FNR8040S3R9NT. Isat clears the floor by only 0.02 A, accepted because the load estimate is near 0.3 A. Datasheet not read; values are catalogue values. Footprint: Inductor_SMD:L_Bourns-SRN6028, the KiCad library pattern for the Bourns SRN6028 series (two 1.6 x 5.7 mm pads at 4.7 mm pitch), swapped on the board and the schematic on 2026-11-05 in place of the Vishay IHLP-2525 pattern left from the earlier part; no copper was attached to L2 yet. No open design in the corpus uses it; lifecycle basis is the JLC catalogue only. Gate: lifecycle Unknown: jlcparts listing lists it, which is a catalogue listing, not a manufacturer status; no manufacturer lifecycle source is configured (no Digi-Key or Mouser key in parts.json), so the gate cannot prove Active; introduction date unknown (no datasheet first date, research report or curated row), so the age rule could not run"
			(at 72.39 16.51 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1 1)
				)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
