		)
		(property "Description" "Four pin crystal, GND on pins 2 and 4"
			(at 394.97 74.93 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1 1)
				)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
		(property "MPN" "K3A240001010"
			(at 394.97 74.93 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1 1)
				)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
		(property "Manufacturer" "KYX"
			(at 394.97 74.93 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1 1)
				)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
		(property "Wright.PickReason" "2026-11-03 Any part (keyword only) x1: needs no electrical constraint. jlcparts Active (catalog status field (JLC/LCSC listing, not the manufacturer)), stock 1373, 0.0625 USD each at 1.  (0 other candidates passed) Chosen because: HSE crystal, 24 MHz, 10 pF load, +/-10 ppm, 30 ohm ESR, -40 to 85 C, SMD3225-4P (stock 1,373 at JLC). 24 MHz is the PLL input the STM32G4 reaches 170 MHz from (24 / 6 x 85 / 2) and matches prior art memirmakar/foc-driver BOM_revB.csv (24 MHz ECS-240-12-37B crystal, 15 pF) and ST's Nucleo-G4 boards. Load capacitors: CL 10 pF with about 4 pF of stray gives 2 x (10 - 4) = 12 pF, so two 12 pF C0G caps. Chosen over the ECS-240-12-37B-7KM (-20 to 70 C only, 45 in stock) for the skateboard's temperature range. A crystal rather than the internal RC is deliberate for UART baud and PWM-timing accuracy. Lifecycle basis is the JLC catalogue only (a generic crystal, no manufacturer statement read); KYX is a lesser-known maker, so any equivalent 24 MHz 10 pF 3225 crystal is an acceptable second source."
