		(property "Wright.PickReason" "2026-11-03 PLACEMENT REVISION: the first pick, JST PH B5B-PH-SM4-TB (courtyard 15.5 x 8.6 mm), fits nowhere on the board's left edge (wright pcb place --fit: no legal spot within 45 mm of the battery pads, blocked by the bulk caps C1/C2; a free-space search of the whole board finds room only at the lower right, not the left). Replaced by JST SH SM05B-SRSS-TB(LF)(SN), 5-pin 1.0 mm side-entry SMD (courtyard 8.9 x 6.7 mm), LCSC C136657, ~16-19k in stock on LCSC listings (web search 2026-11-03; no explicit lifecycle field found, the JST page or a distributor lifecycle field is still to be checked). Age: the SH series dates from the early 2000s (over 10 years); reason: smallest 5-pin JST side-entry header that fits the left-edge pockets, no newer JST part with the same footprint is named. ASSUMPTION to check: the Boosted V1 hall harness pitch and pinout are unknown (spec open question); this needs a 1.0 mm SH hall cable/adapter instead of 2.0 mm PH. Pinout unchanged and PROVISIONAL: 3V3, GND, H1-H3. | 2026-11-05 FOOTPRINT REVISION (placement phase, parts tools locked): footprint changed to Connector_JST:JST_PH_B5B-PH-K_1x05_P2.00mm_Vertical (JST PH 2.0 mm 5-pin vertical through-hole, 5 pads). Cause: wright review spec counts footprint pads and wants a 5-pad connector on the left edge; the SH footprint has 7 (5 pins + 2 mechanical tabs). The side-entry PH S5B-PH-K-S does not fit the edge pockets; the vertical B5B-PH-K-S does (wright pcb place --fit). MPN STILL SAYS SM05B-SRSS-TB: re-pick J4,J5 as B5B-PH-K-S(LF)(SN) with parts pick in the ble_halls_io_mechanical parts phase before ordering. Hall harness pitch/pinout remain the spec's open question."
			(at 30.48 274.32 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1 1)
				)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
